-blank-
^yellow;Antithetical Arts: 1.5 second perfect block time.^white;
^yellow;Passivity, Parted: 5hp blocking power.^white;

''I love cheap whiskey!''

A swig of flammable oil right down yer noggin', then right back out at the would-be Assassin in a wave of flame.

^#D6DFFF;Use to drink, and spit out a short-ranged flame blast.^white;

A remarkably durable Lee-Enfield rifle that can withstand an immense amount of punishment. Shorter than regular spears but can shoot repeatedly unlike most gun-blades.
^orange;Final attack fires a high-powered short-ranged bullet.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Aimed Shot [SHIFT]: Fire an enhanced aimed shot at the cursor | 10s Cooldown.^white;

With access to only scraps and low-quality metals, underground smiths are forced into utilizing ancient techniques to turn them into usable tools. Repeatedly folding metal can help bring out impurities, but there is only so much one can do with something so impure.
^orange;Final strike afflicts 6s SHREDDING (-25% SLASH and BLEED PROC RES) | ^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 45HP STABILITY^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Ki Pulse [SHIFT]: Activating within 2s of a perfect-parry or dodge proc restores 10HP | No cooldown.^reset;

The longbow is a type of bow that can make a fairly large draw thanks to its size and relatively narrow limbs. It is the standard bow weapon for archery playstyles and deals balanced damage with the ammo available, but on-average has lower velocity than bolts.

^#B4DB72;Baseline: No projectile deviation | High Draw: Max projectile speed.^reset;
^orange;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE (all projectiles always hit). CRIT Arrows have different effects based on the arrow.^reset;

A crowbar used by workers.

^orange;When held in the hand, can be used to unlock certain doors. Can be used indefinitely.

^#FFEEC6;Double Striker [SHIFT]: Perform two focused attacks, dealing high THRUST and BLEED DMG | 18s cooldown.^reset;

''I was separated from my group when I stumbled upon another lone Floran. Felt like an eternity till I just started running at him with my bayonet. He spun his spear 'round but it was too late; Knife went deep into his chest. Saw eye-to-eye. Poor soul looked underfed, scrawny. A lot smaller than me. I gave him a final shot to the head.''
Outdated assault rifle used during the late-stages of the USCM-Floran War, chambered in 5.56x45mm STANAG-FEDERATSIYA.
^orange;The Lost: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY^reset;

''The gun does not care for who fired it.''

A pillbox made from thick wooden logs and crewed by a handful of peasants armed with blackpowder rifles. Only two gunners can fire at a time, with assistant loaders handing reloaded firearms to the gunners. Reload times are inconsistent.

^orange;Constructed Building: 45s construction time.^reset;

---
Outdated assault rifle used during the late-stages of the USCM-Floran War, chambered in 5.56x45mm STANAG-FEDERATSIYA.
^orange;The Lost: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY^reset;

Ancient designs for the AKM series were pulled up by desperate colonial home guards. That practice hasn't changed for most, and it still sees use by independent powers unaligned with the Unitans who also predominantly utilize Soviet-style firearms. Uses AK 5.45x39mm Magazines. Cannot use Drum Magazines.
^orange;Vandal: 0.8s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY^reset;

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a questionable one-handed stance.^reset;

The long time standard issue rifle of the German Bundeswehr, used by many colonial troops *right now*. Made a name for itself being a robust & reliable weapon that can be used damn near anywhere. 7.62x51mm is heavy, but you could do much worse than having it come out of a G3. The fact that this & its cousin, the FAL, are still kicking should be a testament to both rifles.

Loads 7.62x51mm BR Magazines.
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''Buried underground on an unknown island, a wealthy noble constructed a crypt in memory of those lost in the Shogunate's war against the Machinarius. His closest friend was erased from history for his ties to a shunned religion.''

^orange;Final strike sends out icicles that fire off forwards a short distance^reset; | ^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 75HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Winter-Pierce [SHIFT]: Leap into the air and stab downwards, firing additional icicle projectiles downwards | 25s Cooldown.

''A lifetime of training for a moment of glory.''

Axemen are warriors who act as melee skirmishers. They open up with a throwing axe before marching towards the front with shields up. Their use can easily disrupt an assault, distracting melee units and preventing ranged units from using their weapons.
^orange;Assault Stance: Designated infantry will move towards enemies and attack them.^reset;

''Javelins are like giant arrows.''

A simple rack equipped with throwing spears. Your typical spearman will carry his large longspear and a much shorter throwing spear for breaking apart enemy shield formations.

^orange;Spearman Bolster: Nearby spearmen gain +100% DMG | Instantly constructed.^reset;

''We pushed ourselves beyond the boundaries of our bodies. We did not simply push ourselves to the limit. We went beyond. It wasn't that they had their flesh torn. It was that they had their souls torn out.''

^orange;Cold-Blooded: 220HP STABILITY | 80% DEF.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user. Cannot perfect-block.^white;

''The spear has been one of humanity's oldest true weapons. There is something primal about this Flesh abomination's interpretation of one of humanity's oldest weapons.''

^orange;Final strike afflicts 6s RENDING (Bleeding deals +20 DMG/s | No effect if not bleeding) at cost of thrust range.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Flesh-Pierce [SHIFT]: Leap into the air and stab downwards, dealing immense DMG | 30s Cooldown.^white;

A shell that launches a flare that descends slowly, illuminating the area for approximately 30s.

Close-ranged shots are capable of dealing ^orange;IGNITION^reset;, but deal significantly reduced direct damage. ^orange;Causes SUPPRESSION on nearby enemies for 30s.^reset;

Unaffected by Weapon Proficiency.

Sometimes pronounced ''Wolfak'' or cynically as ''Well, fuck''. This kit offers a lot of equipment to address the broadest range of conditions. Often part of long-term colonization efforts in hostile environments.

^green;- Restores 400 health/10s | Heal Delay: 2.75s | Immobile Time: 3s
^yellow;Removes ALL BLEEDING.^white;
^orange;- Heals Burn Wounds^white; | ^yellow;- Heals Bruising.^white;
^red;- Heals Blood Loss^white; | ^gray;- Heals Fractures.^white;

Humanity was full of guns like these, believing that these rounds would be the ones adopted across Earth. Ironically, smaller 'intermediate' cartridges would prove to retain significantly more power at range and guns like these fell out of favor.
Loads SCAR-H 7.62x51mm Magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

This gun now fires in 1200 RPM fuller-auto.

Uses Browning HP 9x19mm magazines.

^green;Double Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a comfortable two-handed grip, returning the weapon back to full-auto.^reset;

Demo longsword that fires projectiles and applies effects when swinging.
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.^white;

^yellow;Riposte: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 150HP STABILITY.^reset;
^orange;Hardened Steel: [SHIFT] to hilt bash nearby targets, stunning them for two seconds.^reset;

Concealing a spear is difficult, and to hand these out en-masse would indicate a turf war gone desperate.

^orange;Final strike afflicts 6s RENDING (Bleeding deals +20 DMG/s | No effect if not bleeding).

^#FFEEC6;Precise Strike [SHIFT]: Prepare a singular, focused thrust attack that deals high THRUST and BLEED DMG | 10s cooldown.^white;

A hefty axe forged from the remains of a Glitch champion, styled after his massive battle axe. The Champion himself underwent an excruciating upgrade process to achieve his state.
^orange;Steadfast: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 300HP STABILITY.^reset;
Hold [ALT-FIRE] to parry.
^green;Head-Splitter: Regular attacks inflict additional heavy bleed damage against regular enemies and [GiC] Bosses.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Lord of War: After a throw, press [SHIFT] to forcibly recall the axe. Otherwise, pick it up manually.^reset;

A commission was requested by a Crow-Tengu Chieftain to produce a weapon that could also channel wind magic. Very few could be produced.
^orange;2nd strike DEFLECTS (resist melee) | Final strike grants +30% Movement and DODGE for 2s and deals 2x DMG^reset; | ^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 45HP STABILITY.^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Wind Blast [SHIFT]: Prepare a singular focused attack that sends out a wind blast. Enemies that are sent flying take heavy damage if they hit a wall hard enough | 16s cooldown.^reset;

The legend itself. The M1911 was the brainchild of John Moses Browning, and is one of his most successful & iconic firearm designs, going on to influence nearly all modern centerfire pistols. Adopted by the US in 1911 as a replacement for the Colt Single Action Army, the M1911 would go on to fight in both World Wars and nearly every single major conflict throughout the 20th century & well beyond.
Fires the heavy .45 ACP bullet and holds 7rnds per magazine.
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a versatile one-handed grip.^reset;

''When the term 'machine gun' enters common parlance, the word 'machine' becomes much more sinister.''

Fires the heavy .45 ACP pistol cartridge using unique 30rnd M1A1 stick magazines.

^orange;The Marine: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 30HP STABILITY^reset;

''If I were to pick up this cowering-plate, I would have to put down my second sword,'' a Scotsman thinks. ''And surely that is madness.''

^yellow;Knightly Demolitionist: 0.5s PARRY WINDOW | 5HP BLOCK.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;+50% fire damage resistance on wearer.^white;
^#D6DFFF;+30% explosive damage resistance on wearer.^reset;
^#orange;Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal heightened damage based on the speed of the user.^reset;

''Humanity reveled in their weapons development. But after such illustrious feats, lethargy festered within their genius. Without passion and purpose, there can be no innovation.''

Chambered in 9x18mm. Holds 35 rounds with controllable recoil management for long bursts of fire.

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a two-handed stance.^reset;

''Who are the Resigans? It's where the Alliance of Independent Systems were born. The United Systems were getting too big for their own good and opted to split the nation in half. It saved them, but it can only last so long.''

5.45x39mm Resigan Assault Rifle K-designation, variant 6. Accepts AK 5.45x39mm magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''Soldiers always come in groups, and so should your bullets.''

Despite its haphazard assembly, the makeshift semi-auto pistol proves to be surprisingly reliable in combat, with a rusty barrel, crude trigger, and cobbled-together magazine all working together seamlessly to pack a powerful punch. Chambered in a hefty 7.62x39mm cartridge.

^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a versatile one-handed grip.^reset;

A tainted remnant of the Tyrant Judge, a fragmented avatar of the Great Yamaxanadu.
The Tyrant Judge, as she was so-called, was ultimately a disjointed personality created from the One True Yamaxanadu created to hold the tide of Abyssal forces from outright wiping worlds that had an excess of psychic potential. Tragically, her efforts would often be for naught as humanity would still find a way to worsen their own state through petty conflicts.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

Semi-automatic pistol originally produced by Mauser from 1896 to 1937. Ammo-efficient and packing a punch, but slow to load and jams often.

^orange;Reloads significantly slower than usual.^reset;
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a stable two-handed grip.^reset;

''Most people look at this thing and think it's no better than a piece of junk. They're not wrong, it *is* made from shit. Doesn't mean it's shit though, eh?''

The magazines for these kinds of guns are often custom-made, and thus incompatible with each other. For that purpose, you must load the bullets manually on-the-fly. Loads 7.62x39mm bullets.

^orange;Wrought Havoc: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 150HP STABILITY^reset;

''Thought I'd seen the worst of it after spending an hour fighting one man holed-up in a building. I don't think people understand this but... people tend to not want to die. The man we were meant to kill, fled, but he left behind some of his belongings. That was good enough for us.'' 

Accepts 20 Gauge shells.
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a comfortable two-handed grip.^reset;

''The AI knows. Send a killer to catch a killer. No... No, no! You are not what you were! Whatever you heard, whatever you remember, you are not that, not anymore.''

^#BCBC87;Uses Mk23 SOCOM .45 ACP Magazines.^reset;

^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a versatile one-handed grip.^reset;

^#EA3C0B;Blasting Fire: Shots at close-range deal heavy damage, as well as knocking the enemy and player back^reset; | ^yellow;Cannot hit targets beyond these ranges.^reset;
^orange;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE. CRIT Shots increase pellet DMG by 3x.^reset;
^#EA3C0B;Front-Rank Fire: Shots are packed with large consistent pellets, dealing 5x50 additional damage | Fast reloads.^reset;

Loads Standard Shot ONLY.

''Muh' stoppin' power.''

Fires the heavy .45 ACP bullet and holds 7rnds per magazine.

^orange;Bullets deal ridiculous knockback | Knockback-affected enemies take terrain impact damage dependent on velocity | Cannot one-hand | Cannot use special ammo.^reset;

''Great Sage is dead. Gensokyo must fall.''

^orange;Reloads significantly slower than usual.^reset;
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a stable two-handed grip.^reset;

''''

