''These things are still around? Well, finders keepers as they always say.''

^orange;Slam-Fire: Trigger can be held down to fire at a rapid rate, but recoil recovery is significantly slower than other shotguns.^reset;

^orange;Can jam, unlike other shotguns.^reset;

''Even the lowest wall can buy precious time.''
A low wooden palisade that offers rudimentary cover from ranged attacks. While infantry can maneuver through defenses with little risk by itself, these palisades can delay them as they move through. Pair with defensive units to better protect them whilst opening up enemy melee troops to attack.
^orange;Infantry Defense: Infantry are delayed and unshielded when moving through | Not always a target for enemies | Instantly constructed.^reset;

''I just needed one shot. Pull out this thing and shoot him in the body. It's all I needed to do. So I do. And I miss, twice.''

^yellow;Fires 2 18.5x70mm slug or buckshot rounds^reset; loaded in a break-action fashion.
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to an^reset; impractical ^green;one-handed grip.^reset;

The siege crossbow is a larger variant of the light crossbow, offering greater accuracy and physical power for use at longer distances.
^#B4DB72;Besieger: No projectile deviation | All shots at fastest speed | Very low durability.

^orange;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE (all projectiles always hit). CRIT Bolts have different effects based on the bolt.^reset;

Must have been left behind when the army pulled out. Sadly the poor thing looks like it was sitting in dirt, mud & baking in the sun for about a century give or take before these guys got ahold of it &... did things to it. On the bright side, looks like it can be fixed with enough work!
  Loads any 5.56x45mm STANAG NATO mags I guess
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

The crossbow influenced the medieval battlefield that led to an invigoration of the peasant army. Where the archer required training that was strengthened from childhood, a man could be handed a crossbow with few weeks training.
^#B4DB72;Baseline: Deals base damage of bolts. No specialty, beyond being a fast early crossbow.

^orange;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE (all projectiles always hit). CRIT Bolts have different effects based on the bolt.^reset;

The White Wolves seldom used Greatshields, reserving the heavier equipment for the protection and rescue of lone pups, and to push back against threats to whatever new home they've found among humans.

^#B24A5A;Abyss-Walker: +0.5% HP regeneration when equipped in either hand | 600hp blocking power.^white;  
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

''Everyone always says they can fashion shit from junk from their mother's arse. That they can sooo easily do it. Yeah, so why don't you make it, huh? Fuckin' city-folk...''

^#688686;I SAID GET BACK: Heavy Knockback and Bleeding in every shot.^reset;
^#D6AF8B;Can only use custom Owl-Hunter Bolts.^reset;
^yellow;Heat Overcharging: Direct hits lower enemy attack power by 50%

A fairly long 32rnd 9x19mm stick magazine loaded with Hollow-Point ammunition, which shreds unarmored targets but deals less DMG against even basic armor.

^orange;Hollow Point:^reset;
If enemy TGT has less than 15% Small-Arms or 30% Thrust RES, then apply 3s Bleeding, 1s Rending, and +25 direct BLEED DMG. Deals reduced base DMG. Cannot apply bleed if TGT has armor.

One of the most produced revolvers in history. Smith & Wesson started pumping these out in 1899 & hadn't stopped... that is till they did due to nuclear armageddon. It took some time but eventually the company would bounce back from the fallout & get some juicy contracts from the resurged United States. Police forces on a galactic scale have enjoyed the pistols great reliablity & ease of use for centuries.
Feeds .38 Special Bullets
^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a one-handed grip.^reset;

^red;''Never take a gamble you're not prepared to lose.''^reset;
The Mars-Pattern Assault Plasma Gun saw use hundreds of years ago as an anti-tank infantry weapon for the rich and mighty nations of the past. Most other countries could only dream of affording these weapons platforms.
^orange;0.2% chance for shots to randomly be weaker, up to 53.2% at 0% durability.^reset;

''A Yamaxanadu will write the nature of one's sin on the rod. The worse the sin, the heavier the rod becomes. Those who did many wrong things are beaten many times with equal proportion to their sins.''
^green;Hold [ALT-FIRE] to block.^white;
^orange;Mind-Strikes: 1s STUN, RAMP-UP BOSS-BLEED per combo (up to 4s) and +100 TRUE damage for every attack.^white;
^#D1C8BF;World's Edge: [SHIFT] to release a wide piercing projectile that deals 200 PSYCHIC DMG.^white;

''Going from toting a machine gun... to using a bed pan, and I can't even put my own socks on - that was hard to kind of suck it up.''

The Kurtz Maschinenpistole 5, an extremely popular SMG used by both military & law enforcement chambered in 9x19mm. Holds 35rnds.

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a questionable one-handed stance.^reset;

''Follow me, men! Forward!''

A snub nose double-action revolver accepting .357 (9x33mm) rounds. Marketed to civilians as a small and concealable revolver, the Super Eagle-14 was designed to be used within close quarters. It has recently seen use in the hands of People's Army Commissars, and commonly used as a symbol of authority.

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a one-handed grip.^reset;

An oval scutum shield that can be aimed to provide cover against primitive missiles (but not against contemporary rocket-propelled munitions). The first depictions of the scutum were by the Este culture in the 8th century BC, and subsequently spread to the Etruscans, Illyrians, Celts, and Italians.

^green;Attacking Testudo: Can be aimed | 100hp blocking power (npc).^white;  
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

Rifle that's been with you since you first served in the military. Its parts have been replaced dozens of times and gone through hell and back.

Loads G3 7.62x51mm Magazines.
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

A dull remnant of the Ex-Cultist, a man who imbued himself with otherworldly powers for the sake of survival.

The Ex-Cultist was a rather unremarkable man on a personal level. He did not care for any specific goal and was mostly interested in just collecting shiny trinkets and killing off anyone who he considered was worthy of fighting in a duel, which was more of a spectacle than a life-threatening duel.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''Some people will say to just get a better gun. We would, if we could.''

Uses 9x19mm Browning magazines.
^orange;Absurdly high base accuracy and hit chance.^reset;
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''We had vowed to slay this false god. Yet, this promise was not more than a coerced pledge. What difference does it make, which master we serve? We will serve all the same.''

A versatile weapon combining a spear and axe, allowing for precise thrusts, slashing, and armor-piercing stabs.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Counter-Brace [SHIFT]: Brace for an attack. If hit, respond with an ARMOR-PIERCING SPIKE that deals THRUST and BLEED DMG.^white;

''Protectors freak the fuck out when they see this coming their way. If I can't kill them, then I'll make them feel every second of their death. Yeah, run you little shits! Run!''
^#D96045;Whirligig Whirly-Gig: When held out, deal rapid contact damage but no knockback and cannot rotate aim when held out | Deals heavy bleeding on hit.
^#D6DFFF;Perseverance: [SHIFT] to channel the weapon's spirit, momentarily stunning nearby enemies. Gain total knockback resistance for 20s | 30s cooldown.^reset;

''The strongest took the spoils, and we fell down at their shoes.''

^orange;Heretic: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 180HP STABILITY | 60% DEF.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Full Force Forward!: +25% HIT CHANCE and ACCURACY with [EWS] guns whilst equipped in either hand.^white;
^red;New Age Movement: Energy regeneration crippled whilst equipped.^reset;

''The East placated with tribute and the West defeated with our faith.''

^orange;Final strike afflicts 4s WINDED (-25% BLUNT RES and Warrior DMG).
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 30HP STABILITY^white;
^#FFEEC6;Nevsky's Loyalty [SHIFT]: Slam the mace into the ground and call upon ancient soldiers to attack enemies in melee with the bearer, calculating MAX HP for duration | Duration = BASE 5s + ((CURRENT MAX HP - 100)/2) | Effect expires if holstered | CD = 30s + duration.^white;

''Chaos and cruelty took hold after the Great Barrier imploded, leaving Gensokyo open to the ravages of the Outside World, or Earth, as we now know it. I am not a murderer, but to be defenseless is to be foolish.''
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.4s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY.^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Stake Blaster Combo [SHIFT]: Fire three gun-blasts in quick succession to deal rapid damage. Last shot fires a Youkai-Stake that rapidly deals BLEED damage over 3s | 40s cooldown.^white;

''In forty minutes, people will be shooting at these 19 year old boys. And they will shoot back, and they will kill. That is the law of war: if you don't kill first, they'll kill you. We didn't invent this law.''

Uses AK 5.45x39mm Magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

20rnd magazine for the FG42. Loaded with a powerful pure incendiary mixture.

^orange;Incendiary:^reset;
Chance to proc 5s IGNITION (Base 70% chance, each 1% of THERMAL RES reduces proc chance by 1%) | +40 THERMAL DMG | Loses Wall-Piercing ability.

12rnd 11.43x23mm (.45 ACP) magazine for the MK23 pistol. Loaded with Hollow-Point ammunition which shreds unarmored targets but deals less DMG against even basic armor.

^orange;Hollow Point:^reset;
If enemy TGT has less than 15% Small-Arms or 30% Thrust RES, then apply 3s Bleeding, 1s Rending, and +25 direct BLEED DMG. Deals reduced base DMG. Cannot apply bleed if TGT has armor.

''Every part of human history is buried under a scorching sky set ablaze by our darkest demons and drowned under an ocean of the blood of our brightest angels.''

^orange;50% of DMG converted to THERMAL | 2nd strike DEFLECTS (resist melee) | Final strike afflicts 4s IGNITION.^reset;
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 45HP STABILITY.^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Enflamed Strike [SHIFT]: Perform a heavy upper slash, spewing flames a distance forwards that afflict IGNITION | 16s cooldown.^reset;

30rnd 11.43x23mm (.45) magazine for the M1A1 Thompson. Loaded with Hollow-Point ammunition which shreds unarmored targets but deals less DMG against even basic armor.

^orange;Hollow Point:^reset;
If enemy TGT has less than 15% Small-Arms or 30% Thrust RES, then apply 3s Bleeding, 1s Rending, and +25 direct BLEED DMG. Deals reduced base DMG. Cannot apply bleed if TGT has armor.

''I was given a choice: to kneel before the executioner's axe or their queen. An easy choice. For years, I wore her sigil and repeated all the oaths. But I always knew one day, no matter how many honors were bestowed upon me, I would escape.''
The longsword is a quick, effective, and versatile weapon capable of deadly thrusts, slices, and cuts.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 75HP STABILITY.^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Hard Striker [SHIFT]: Prepare a singular focused attack, dealing high SLASH and BLUNT DMG | 12s cooldown.^reset;

Julian's forays into the occult led him to a place beyond the veils of the world. To Whisperfog, a land shrouded in eternal fog. His reward was his very being crushed into nothingness as a demon inhabited his armor.
^orange;2nd strike DEFLECTS (resist melee) | Final strike rains arrows around the wielder.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 45HP STABILITY.^reset;
^#FFEEC6;Arms Rain [SHIFT]: Strike with a heavy-hitting slash that summons weapons to rain down around the bearer | 40s cooldown.^reset;

''Just a piece of wood. That's what those stupid Protectors in their armchairs typing away on their computers would say. They don't have to do what I do to survive.''

^orange;Hot-Blooded: 3500HP STABILITY | 40% DEF.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Shield Rush: Moving at mere running speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage and ^orange;STUN^#D6DFFF; based on the speed of the user. 2-second cooldown per stun.^white;

''I have outlived that care that curries public favour or dreads the public frown... let the hand of law strike me down if it will, but I ask that my story be heard and considered.''

Fires .36 Cal Paper Cartridges.

^orange;Reloads significantly slower than usual.^reset;
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a stable two-handed grip.^reset;

''The fight begins with the fog of war.''

A small watchtower with a barely-trained peasant acting as a spotter. Whilst highly ineffective as an actual defensive unit, the additional points this building can generate could mean the difference between a secure front or a lost battle.
^orange;Field Spotter: Spots distant enemies, passively generating Requisition Points | Extremely weak to melee | 30s construction time.^reset;

Close Air Support Coordinator Beacon, activating on impact | ^orange;Requires open space | If it cannot be called in, the beacon is refunded near where it was originally detonated.^reset;

^orange;WP Bomb + Strafe:^reset; Calls in a Goshawk fightercraft to strafe the beacon impact zone with machineguns before dropping a White Phosphorus Bomb on the target zone.^reset;

^red;White Phosphorus is indiscriminate.^reset;

''You're still a routine in the machine. An operator in the calculation. One of the millions of dogs, fetching a million bones, over and over. Searching for memories you've lost a thousand times.''

